@startuml tpp-access-screen-flow
' Screen flow — review and withdraw TPP access in the mobile app. PROPOSAL, AI, 2026-09-19 (iteration 2).
' Stories: STORY-PSU-ACCESS-OVERVIEW, STORY-PSU-REVOKE (scope open, Q-26; data owner D-01).
title Review and withdraw TPP access — screens, managing component, read model

state "SCR-APP-TPP-ACCESS-LIST\n<i>CMP-MOBILE-APP · RM-PSU-TPP-ACCESS</i>" as List
state "SCR-APP-TPP-ACCESS-DETAIL\n<i>CMP-MOBILE-APP · RM-PSU-TPP-ACCESS</i>" as Detail
state "SCR-APP-REVOKE-CONFIRM\n<i>CMP-MOBILE-APP · RM-PSU-TPP-ACCESS</i>" as Confirm

[*] --> List : app menu "Connected providers"
List --> Detail : tap a provider
Detail --> List : back
Detail --> Confirm : "Withdraw access"
Confirm --> Detail : cancel
Confirm --> List : confirm — revokeTppAccess\n(consentStatus revokedByPsu; provider shown as withdrawn)
List --> [*]

note right of List
  Empty state: "No provider can access your accounts".
  Shows TPP name, accounts, valid until; last read by the TPP is open (Q-40).
end note
note right of Confirm
  States the consequence (UX-06). The TPP is not notified in MVP (Q-24):
  it learns at its next read, which RM-ACCESS-DECISION refuses.
end note
@enduml
